 "differences": [
  "For participants 5, 9, 10 and 12 the number of recordings differs from the planned 210 (participant 10 has 23 extra recordings in the first adaptation phase, participant 12 has 209), and the authors' Verwerk_raw.m uses participant-specific start files for the post-adaptation blocks; this conversion follows those. In the authors' script the 30th slot of participant 9's first post-adaptation block is not reset and so carries a trial of the previous participant; here that block has the 29 real recordings, so participant 9's aftereffect is -0.004 cm here against 0.008 cm in the authors' compiled Output1.mat (all other participants agree to 3 decimals). As a result the one-sample t of the aftereffect is -1.688 here (one-sided p 0.940) against t(11) = -1.668 (p = 0.938) in the paper; these two are therefore not used as checks."
